mso-border-bottom-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;">
                    <p class=MsoNormal><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:12.0000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋"><p>This course primarily centers on the architecture and protocols of the Internet, while also incorporating content on data communication. It discusses the basic concepts and fundamental principles of computer networks from both theoretical and practical perspectives, covering the foundational issues, mainstream network protocols, current cutting-edge advancements. The main topics include: network applications, the transport layer, the network layer, the data link layer, the physical layer.</p></font></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
                </td>
            </tr>
